[Music]  i became leader in june 3rd of june i  was uh born in a small village outside  of favisham i went to work in london  i was elected in 2015  and  i was re-elected again in 2019. i've  played the sport all my life i think  sports really important i play  football for south england played hockey  for  handball and cliftonville and i play  golf now at northland and had been  played at westgate  being the leader i mean i had to hit the  ground running obviously it's not easy  when you come in mid-term the main thing  really is that i like to get out and  meet the people to see what the  communities are up to  i treat the residents of sanet in the  way that i used to in my previous jobs  the shareholders we were accountable to  shareholders and i sort of  think of residents as  shareholders of  of the district  my main focus is on  um  trying to  leverage as much inward investment into  the thana area because i believe that  we've got some golden opportunities here  and we have to get that investment in  that's the whole point of the government  with the  with the leveling up funds with the  margate town deal with the high street  funds  this is just really to show  the big investors that look the  government's willing to invest in it and  only  a couple of weeks ago  i met along with the  mp and the deputy leader  the secretary of state  robert generic came here we met him at  the station we walked in along the  seafront we showed him the old town we  walked up the high street  and just exampled about how this is the  sort of area that the money the  government are injecting will help  i recently went to ramsgate football  club who were running the  hab programme  it was quite humbling when i walked in  there  and there's all 200 children all running  about in there and it's quite humbling  to think that you know this is all going  on and  and i don't think people quite realize  how much effort you know what they put  into it to run it to run these clubs and  there's a lot of the community that come  together with that there's and the  community in thana is fantastic you know  we have people that go out and regularly  litter pick  um they're all unsung heroes you know  and unpaid heroes but they just like  their area to look good  [Music]  very early in my um  role as leader was the major incident  with southern water occurred with the  failure of the fullness pumping station  and like all the residents and the  businesses of thanet i was totally  outraged at  that this had happened yet again  so  on the sunday following um i said to my  wife i'm going to write to the chief  executive of southern water and just  tell him exactly how i feel  and  demand that he comes down to a meeting  i  basically demanded not what  what i would call compensation but i  just felt that  as a gesture of goodwill to senate  district council and the distress that  it's caused the the area  um that i felt that they should make a  compensation payment so um  that has was agreed and i'm pleased to  say that the funds have been transferred  into the thani district council's  account and  that has been ring fenced and i will put  that to to good to good causes within  margate ramsgate and broadstairs to the  benefit of the residents i also asked  for um the  chief executive of southern water to  come and address a member's briefing  which he did on monday  and um  again it was um  he was a he was able to answer the  questions that  that members obviously have been asking  since the incident i think that it was a  it was a good and constructive meeting  and also he outlined the southern waters  plans for the um infrastructure and the  improvements to the infrastructure for  thanning  so that hopefully we don't ever have to  experience this again  [Music]

